    "fileId": 38042,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Choroidal melanoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "The typical presentation of a choroidal melanoma on MRI is shown. The mass appears isointense to the choroid on T1-weighted images and enhances after contrast administration. On T2-weighted images it is slightly hyperintense compared with the extraocular muscles. Posterior and anterior to the mass, small retinal detachments can be seen, which do not enhance on T1-weighted images with contrast and are slightly hypointense compared with the melanoma on T2-weighted images. On perfusion-weighted imaging, the choroidal melanoma shows a typical washout curve.",
    "source": "Jan-Willem M. Beenakker",
